# Build-context allowlist for docker/probe.Dockerfile specifically --
# picked up automatically by Docker as "<Dockerfile>.dockerignore" instead
# of the repo-root .dockerignore whenever this exact Dockerfile is built
# via `-f docker/probe.Dockerfile`.
#
# The repo-root .dockerignore was written for docker/worker.Dockerfile
# only (its own header says so) and excludes the whole scripts/ directory
# -- correct for the worker image, but it also blocks probe.Dockerfile's
# own COPY scripts/connectivity_probe.py step, since .dockerignore applies
# to the entire build context regardless of which Dockerfile is in use.
# Rather than loosening the worker's own ignore file, this probe-specific
# allowlist excludes everything by default and re-includes only the two
# paths this Dockerfile actually needs, plus their parent directories
# (Docker's exclusion of a directory blocks re-inclusion of a file inside
# it unless the directory itself is also re-included first).
**
!docker/
!docker/probe.Dockerfile
!scripts/
!scripts/connectivity_probe.py
